---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  locale="en"
  title="2026 Quant Competition | Project"
  description="Research and Paper execution engineering for the 2026 Hong Kong Quant Competition."
>
  <header class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">2026 · SYSTEMATIC RESEARCH &amp; EXECUTION</p>
    <h1>From strategy research to auditable execution.</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      A research and execution engineering project for the Hong Kong Quant Competition,
      focused on data timing, portfolio risk, broker interfaces, and Paper validation.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="https://github.com/runchengxie/2026-quant-competition">
      View project repository
    </a>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">WHAT THE CODE DOES</p>
      <h2>A concrete handoff, safety, and audit path</h2>
      <p>
        Research and execution connect through versioned target and lineage files. The
        repository validates that handoff, plans portfolio changes, and keeps broker
        activity behind Paper-first safety checks.
      </p>
      <div class="cards">
        <article>
          <h3>1. Validate the handoff</h3>
          <p>
            The execution runner reads <code>targets.json</code> and its lineage record,
            validates the market and portfolio, and calculates rebalance intents against
            supplied holdings.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>2. Apply Paper safeguards</h3>
          <p>
            Preflight checks require Paper and dry-run settings and check target weights
            against the configured single-name limit. IBKR event mapping is covered by local tests; a complete
            supervised Paper order lifecycle has not yet been verified.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>3. Keep an audit trail</h3>
          <p>
            An append-only event journal supports duplicate protection and projection
            rebuilds, while reconciliation compares journaled orders with broker state.
            Tests and GitHub Actions run without provider credentials or a live broker.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">CURRENT STATUS</p>
      <h2>Implemented foundations; validation still in progress</h2>
      <p>
        The codebase also contains experimental Hong Kong and international ETF research
        baselines. The team has not selected or registered a competition strategy.
        AIVIX and Index One permissions, point-in-time data coverage, and their role in a
        reproducible strategy comparison remain under evaluation. No performance result
        is presented as verified.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reusable USD accounting for cash equities and ETFs is implemented in quant-platform,
        with fixed quantities, cash, FX and transaction costs checked by synthetic tests.
        Connecting it to released historical data is the next research integration step;
        total returns and futures settlement remain separate work.
        <a href="https://github.com/runchengxie/2026-quant-competition/blob/main/docs/operations/usd-ledger-delivery-2026-10-03.md">
          Read the accounting delivery update
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="schedule">
      <p class="eyebrow">COMPETITION</p>
      <h2>Competition dates</h2>
      <p>According to the organizer's public rules published on 2026-09-23. Times are Hong Kong time.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Registration deadline: 2026-10-23 at 23:59</li>
        <li>Trading period: 2026-10-26 00:00 through 2027-01-27 06:00</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="https://fundconnecthk.com/quant-league/legal/competition-rules/">
        Read the organizer's public rules
      </a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE</p>
      <h2>Publication status</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        Unit tests and repository CI cover the local validation and safety code. Paper
        read-only IBKR API connectivity, selected contract qualification and daily history
        requests have local evidence. Order submission, cancellation, fills, restart
        recovery and reconciliation still need a supervised end-to-end run.
        No competition or Paper performance results have passed review for
        publication, so this site displays no return figures.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <span>Research project · Paper-first</span>
    <span>Not investment advice or a solicitation to trade.</span>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
